---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Aaron Holmes | Business Systems, Automation & Integrations"
  description="Business systems and automation specialist focused on internal tooling, SaaS integrations, REST APIs, workflow automation, technical implementation, and AI-enabled operations."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero container">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        Business Systems · Internal Tooling · Automation · Integrations
      </p>

      <h1>I turn real business processes into reliable systems.</h1>

      <p class="intro">
        I build and improve business systems, internal tooling, automations, and
        integrations that connect people, processes, data, and SaaS platforms.
        My work spans process discovery, workflow automation, CRM architecture,
        REST APIs and webhooks, technical implementation, production
        troubleshooting, data quality, documentation, training, and AI-assisted
        workflows.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-links">
        <a class="primary-link" href="#projects">Selected work</a>
        <a href="/Aaron_Holmes_Resume.pdf" download>Download résumé</a>
        <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
        <a href="#skills">Technical toolkit</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="projects" class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">Selected technical work</p>

      <div class="project-grid">
        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">Production automation architecture</p>
          <h2>Scaling & Stabilizing a High-Volume Automation Environment</h2>
          <p>
            Reverse-engineered an inherited ecosystem of CRM workflows, custom
            functions, Zapier automations, APIs, document services, and telecom
            integrations. Identified repeated logic, unnecessary lookups, hidden
            dependencies, and failure points while improving logging,
            documentation, and maintainability.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">
            Zapier · Zoho CRM · Zoho Flow · Deluge · APIs · Production Support
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">Workflow architecture</p>
          <h2>Duplicate Processing Redesign</h2>
          <p>
            Replaced fragmented duplicate logic with a centralized decision
            process covering normalized matching, stage and product rules,
            ownership and supplier behavior, exceptions, and a 30-day duplicate
            window. Audited roughly 300 recent records after rollout.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">
            Zoho CRM · Deluge · Workflow Design · Data Quality · Automation
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">API integration</p>
          <h2>Healthcare Eligibility Integration</h2>
          <p>
            Built a custom multi-endpoint REST API integration for insurance
            eligibility workflows, including authentication and token management,
            request and response handling, payer and patient normalization, data
            mapping, CRM updates, and failure handling.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">
            REST APIs · Authentication · JSON · Data Mapping · Zapier · CRM
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">Systems implementation</p>
          <h2>New Product-Line Systems Implementation</h2>
          <p>
            Led systems implementation for a new compression-garment product line,
            translating operational requirements into coordinated changes across intake,
            CRM workflows, product and supplier logic, document generation, and downstream
            fulfillment. Tested the end-to-end process, resolved rollout issues, and
            supported the transition into production.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">
            Requirements Analysis · Process Mapping · CRM · Workflow Automation ·
            Document Automation · Testing & Validation
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="additional-work">
        <h2>Additional work</h2>
        <p>
          Other projects include healthcare CRM and intake automation for Ask Your
          Primary, workflow and enterprise support for the TixWork B2B SaaS
          platform, securities-lending intake and data-enrichment automation, and
          automated content-ingestion and classification systems for TheRedZone.org.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="experience" class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">Experience</p>

      <div class="role-block">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h2>Business Systems Automation</h2>
            <p class="role-company">Lincoln Health Supply</p>
          </div>

          <p class="role-meta">Healthcare · DME/HME · Remote · 2025–2026</p>
        </div>

        <p class="role-summary">
          Owned and modernized a large production business-systems environment
          supporting patient intake, insurance eligibility, prescriptions, medical
          records, documents, orders, fulfillment, and customer communications.
          Worked directly with operations leadership to translate real business
          requirements into reliable CRM workflows, integrations, automation, data
          controls, and internal tooling.
        </p>

        <ul class="experience-list">
          <li>
            Reverse-engineered and supported a large inherited production
            environment spanning 400+ CRM workflows, roughly 150 custom functions,
            ~15 Zoho Flows, and hundreds of Zapier automations. Analyzed an
            environment processing approximately 500,000 Zapier tasks per month to
            identify failure points, redundant lookups, repeated logic, and
            opportunities to improve reliability and maintainability.
          </li>

          <li>
            Designed and deployed a centralized duplicate-processing system with
            normalized email/DOB matching, product and stage rules, ownership and
            supplier handling, exceptions, and a 30-day duplicate window. Audited
            and remediated roughly 300 recent records after rollout.
          </li>

          <li>
            Built a custom multi-endpoint pVerify REST API integration handling
            authentication and token management, requests and responses, payer and
            patient normalization, data mapping, and CRM updates for healthcare
            eligibility workflows.
          </li>

          <li>
            Led systems implementation for a new compression-garment product line,
            translating operational requirements into changes across intake, CRM,
            document generation, supplier routing, and downstream fulfillment
            workflows; tested the process and resolved rollout issues.
          </li>

          <li>
            Improved the supportability of inherited systems through logging,
            failure alerts, traceability, SOPs, and technical documentation;
            supported AI-assisted extraction from inbound medical documentation and
            trained another employee to maintain the environment independently.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role-block">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h2>Business Systems & Automation Consultant</h2>
            <p class="role-company">AviKaiDo</p>
          </div>

          <p class="role-meta">Project-based engagements · 2015–Present</p>
        </div>

        <p class="role-summary">
          Deliver business systems, automation, integration, data, and web solutions
          across healthcare, financial services, B2B SaaS, media, real estate, and
          small-business environments. Work directly with clients and users to
          understand operational problems, identify the real requirements behind a
          request, design practical solutions, troubleshoot production issues, and
          explain technical decisions in clear business language.
        </p>

        <ul class="experience-list">
          <li>
            Support integrations, workflow automation, enterprise operations, and
            sales support for TixWork, a B2B operations SaaS platform deployed
            across 100+ restaurant locations.
          </li>

          <li>
            Designed healthcare CRM and integration workflows for Ask Your Primary,
            including QR-based pharmacy intake, patient-data mapping, and
            fax-to-record automation connecting intake data with downstream
            operational systems.
          </li>

          <li>
            Built lead-intake, market-data enrichment, prospecting, and
            document-generation workflows for international securities-backed
            lending, combining borrower and ticker data with market history,
            financial metrics, and business rules.
          </li>

          <li>
            Developed automated content-ingestion and classification workflows and
            diagnosed recurring production application-performance problems for
            digital publishing projects.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="skills" class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">Technical toolkit</p>

      <div class="skills-grid">
        <div>
          <h2>Business Systems & Automation</h2>
          <p>
            Internal Tooling · Systems Analysis · Business Process Automation ·
            Workflow Automation · Workflow Orchestration · Technical Implementation ·
            Requirements Analysis & Discovery · Process Mapping · Solution Design ·
            Production Support
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>APIs & Integration</h2>
          <p>
            REST APIs · Webhooks · JSON · API Authentication · Bearer Tokens · Data
            Mapping · Data Normalization · Request/Response Troubleshooting ·
            Third-Party Integrations
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>Platforms & Tools</h2>
          <p>
            Zapier · Zoho CRM / Zoho One · Zoho Flow · Deluge · pVerify · Telnyx /
            Phaxio · Google Workspace · Document & PDF Automation
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>Operations & Reliability</h2>
          <p>
            Root-Cause Analysis · Data Quality · Deduplication · Logging · Failure
            Alerts · Traceability · Technical Documentation · SOPs · User Training &
            Enablement · Tool/Vendor Evaluation
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>AI-Enabled Workflows</h2>
          <p>
            AI-Assisted Automation · OpenAI-Assisted Data Extraction · Structured
            Information Extraction · Human-in-the-Loop Workflow Design
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="building-card">
          <h2>Currently Building</h2>
          <p>
            n8n · Python · SQL · JavaScript · Git / GitHub · AWS · AI Agents & Tool
            Calling
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">How I work</p>

      <h2>Understand the process before automating it.</h2>

      <p>
        Automation works best when it reflects how a business actually operates,
        not just how the process looks on paper.
      </p>

      <p>
        I start by learning the people, systems, data, exceptions, workarounds, and
        constraints behind a workflow. Then I look for the simplest reliable
        solution: configuration, automation, integration, internal tooling, a
        reusable function, or sometimes a process change instead of more software.
      </p>

      <p>
        I care about what happens after launch too: failure handling, logging,
        documentation, supportability, user adoption, and whether someone other
        than the original builder can understand the system six months later.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">Where I fit</p>

      <h2>Business operations and technology, connected.</h2>

      <p>
        I’m interested in remote roles at the intersection of business operations
        and technology, including Business Systems, Internal Tooling, Automation,
        Systems Integration, Technical Implementation, Solutions Engineering, and
        Technical Customer Success.
      </p>

      <p>
        I’m particularly interested in teams using APIs, SaaS platforms, workflow
        automation, and AI to solve operational problems where strong technical
        communication matters as much as the tooling itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section container contact-section">
      <p class="section-label">Contact</p>

      <h2>Have a complicated systems problem? Let’s talk.</h2>

      <p>
        I’m interested in remote opportunities involving business systems,
        automation, integrations, implementation, and technical customer work, as
        well as consulting projects where a messy process needs to become a
        maintainable system.
      </p>

      <div class="contact-links">
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: 5rem 4.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-label,
  .project-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
  }

  .hero-links,
  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-link {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .section {
    width: min(calc(100% - 2rem), var(--content-width));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section > h2,
  .role-header h2,
  .project-card h2,
  .skills-grid h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .section > h2 {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
  }

  .section > p:not(.section-label) {
    max-width: var(--reading-width);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .role-block + .role-block {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .role-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .role-header h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
  }

  .role-company,
  .role-meta {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .role-summary {
    max-width: 820px;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  .experience-list {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .experience-list li + li {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .project-grid,
  .skills-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .project-card,
  .skills-grid > div {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.85rem;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .project-card h2,
  .skills-grid h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }

  .project-card p,
  .skills-grid p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .project-tech {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .additional-work {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  .additional-work h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  .additional-work p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .building-card {
    border-style: dashed !important;
  }

  .contact-section {
    padding-bottom: 6rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 800px) {
    .project-grid,
    .skills-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero {
      padding-block: 3.5rem;
    }

    .role-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .section {
      padding-block: 3rem;
    }

    .role-block + .role-block {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding-top: 3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
